# ThreadSanitizer suppressions — keep this file SHORT and keep every entry
# justified. A suppression is a claim that we understand a report better than
# the tool does, and that claim should be rare.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The seqlock payload copy in src/modules/chain/dsp/chain_loader.c
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The chain loader passes a module name from the SPI audio callback to the
# loader thread through a seqlock. The SPI thread MUST NOT block — an RT thread
# waiting on a lock held by a SCHED_OTHER thread is unbounded priority
# inversion — so the writer never waits and the reader retries instead.
#
# A seqlock reader deliberately reads bytes that may be concurrently written,
# then re-reads the sequence counter and DISCARDS what it read if the counter
# moved. The validation is what makes it correct. TSan sees the copy but has no
# way to see the validation that follows it, so it reports a race. This is the
# well-known seqlock blind spot, not a defect in the handshake.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the two one-line copy helpers rather than to
# loader_read_request / chain_loader_request_synth, so a genuine race anywhere
# else in the request path is still reported. That is why those helpers exist
# and why they must not be inlined back.
race:seqlock_read_payload
race:seqlock_write_payload
